**Describe the bug**
In `HttpSecurityRecorder#authenticationMechanismHandler`, `authenticator.sendChallenge` is called:
```
if (throwable instanceof AuthenticationFailedException) {
    authenticator.sendChallenge(event, new Runnable() {
        @Override
        public void run() {
            event.response().end();
        }
    });
} 
```

In `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpAuthenticator#sendChallenge`:
```
public CompletionStage<Void> sendChallenge(RoutingContext routingContext, Runnable closeTask) {
    return mechanism.sendChallenge(routingContext).thenRun(closeTask);
}
```

If the `CompletionStage` returned by `mechanism.sendChallenge` is exceptional, the `thenRun` method won't be invoked, when means that the `closeTask` is never executed. 

**To Reproduce**
Implement a custom `io.quarkus.vertx.http.runtime.security.HttpAuthenticationMechanism` and `io.quarkus.security.identity.IdentityProvider`:

```
@ApplicationScoped
public class HttpAuthenticationMechanismImpl implements HttpAuthenticationMechanism {

    @Override
    public CompletionStage<SecurityIdentity> authenticate(RoutingContext context, IdentityProviderManager identityProviderManager) {
        return identityProviderManager.authenticate(new TokenAuthenticationRequest(new TokenCredential("foo", "bar")));
    }

    @Override
    public CompletionStage<ChallengeData> getChallenge(RoutingContext context) {
        return failedFuture(new UnsupportedOperationException());
    }
}

@ApplicationScoped
public class IdentityProviderImpl implements IdentityProvider<TokenAuthenticationRequest> {

    @Override
    public Class<TokenAuthenticationRequest> getRequestType() {
        return TokenAuthenticationRequest.class;
    }

    @Override
    public CompletionStage<SecurityIdentity> authenticate(TokenAuthenticationRequest request, AuthenticationRequestContext context) {
        return failedFuture(new AuthenticationFailedException());
    }
}
```

